    </section>
    </content>
    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001">
    <term>constructivism</term>
    <meaning>theory that says learners construct knowledge rather than just passively take in information</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00002">
    <term>educational psychology</term>
    <meaning>subfield of psychology that examines the educational process and student outcomes from a psychological perspective, with the goal of explaining achievement gaps</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00003">
    <term>stereotype threat</term>
    <meaning>phenomenon where individuals experience anxiety or fear of confirming negative stereotypes about their social group, which can impair their performance in academic or other achievement-related tasks</meaning>
    </definition>
    </glossary>
    </document>